# {{.Name}}

An `ext.StorageDriver` plugin scaffolded by `alist plugin new`. Fill in
`driver.go`'s `List`/`Link`/`Get` (and any other capabilities you declare)
with real logic against your storage backend, then keep `plugin.json` and
`i18n/*.json` in sync — see below.

## Layout

- `driver.go` — the driver: `Manifest()` (kept equivalent to `plugin.json`)
  and the `ext.StorageDriver` methods
- `main.go` — `grpcplugin.Serve(...)`, the gRPC plugin entrypoint
- `plugin.json` — the manifest, generated from the same data as
  `Manifest()`; keep them in sync (hand-edit both, or regenerate a scratch
  copy with `alist plugin new` and diff)
- `i18n/en.json`, `i18n/zh-CN.json` — bundled translations for the
  `Info.Additional` config fields (`field.<name>.label` / `field.<name>.help`
  keys); run `alist plugin i18n --dir .` after adding/renaming fields
- `pack.sh` / `serve.sh` — build, sign, package, and locally serve the plugin
- `go.mod` — module `{{.Module}}`{{if .ExtPath}}, with a local `replace` to
  the alist-ext SDK checkout at `{{.ExtPath}}` (only needed while iterating
  on unreleased local SDK changes — drop the replace to build against the
  tagged `github.com/AlistGo/alist-ext` release){{else}}, requiring the
  published `github.com/AlistGo/alist-ext {{.ExtRequire}}` module; if you
  need to develop against unreleased local SDK changes instead, add
  `replace github.com/AlistGo/alist-ext => /path/to/alist/ext` to `go.mod`
  yourself, or re-run `alist plugin new` with `--ext-path
  /path/to/alist/ext`{{end}}

## Build

```bash
go build -o dist/plugin .
```

## Package + sign + serve

```bash
./pack.sh          # build, genkey, sign, pack -> dist/{{.Slug}}-{{.Version}}.tar.gz + dist/index.json
./serve.sh &        # serve dist/ at http://127.0.0.1:8767/
```

`pack.sh` shells out to the hidden `alist plugin genkey|sign|pack` commands
(override the binary with `ALIST_BIN=...` if `alist` isn't on `PATH`). Import
`http://127.0.0.1:8767/index.json` as a plugin source, trust
`dist/pubkey.hex`, then install `{{.ID}}` through the usual extension install
gateway.

## i18n

Config-form field translations live in `i18n/<lang>.json`
(`field.<name>.label` / `field.<name>.help`). After editing
`Info.Additional` in `driver.go`, run:

```bash
alist plugin i18n --dir .            # fills in missing keys, keeps existing translations
alist plugin i18n --dir . --check    # CI: exits non-zero if any key is missing
```
